{
 "translation": "One day the committee members also went out to campaign in the evening and eventually reached the stronghold of the conservatives. Outside the temple, around a peepal tree, several devotees were sitting on a cement platform, and the story of the Ramayana was being narrated. Narayan Baba was narrating that part of the Ramayana where a washerman had expelled his wife from the house and had said, \"I am not King Ramachandra who would take back Sita even after she lived with Ravana for so many years.\" And Ramachandraji had expelled the supremely chaste Sita from the house. In such a situation, when she was pregnant, could there be any greater proof of Ramraj? Narayan Baba said, \"This is Ramraj, in which even the words of a washerman are viewed with such respect.\"",
